Z||000000||Wade87GT||11-16-1999||03:23 PM||||I've looked at a lot of Fiero web sites and this is the most informative of all. I was recently able to find the source of my high idling (2000 - 3500 RPM) problem by picking up tips from your many knowledgeable members. As a new member, but long term owner/maintainer (bought our '87 GT in Dec. of '89 with 11,000 miles on it, now has 138,000), I hope to add my assistance in return. Also Cliff, I was stationed at Soesterberg AB during the late Eighties and my Wife is from Zeist. I've returned often enough to miss your Beer (and so much more) but not your gas prices.||||reg||14
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||11-16-1999||06:22 PM||||Hey Wade! Yes, I agree we probably have the best beers in the world, although I must admit I have recently switched from Heineken to Corona.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Anyway, Soesterberg is a nice area, lots of forest and relatively quiet compared to the "randstad". Holland is a great place to visit - just not so great to live...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Great having you on board!||||reg||1
